{{-- Document-owning layout for the auth pages (login, register):
     noindex, no nav/footer, centered card. The stylesheet is the union
     of the two pages' formerly-duplicated blocks (.hint is register's;
     the passkey icon / .row-between / .hide are login's — harmless on
     both). Pages extend this and fill ONE section, content (the card
     plus the page's scripts, verbatim); title/description/robots are
     declared via useSeoMeta in each page's server script. Theme pre-paint
     script placement mirrors layouts/status.stx (layouts do not strip
     a leading script the way partials do). --}}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    {{-- Favicons + fonts come from config/ui.ts app.head. --}}
    {{-- Title/description/robots come from each page's useSeoMeta call
         (stx-standards 04); the framework splices them in server-side. --}}
    {{-- The pre-paint theme script is app.colorMode in config/ui.ts now. --}}
    {{-- window.stacksPasskey, for login's passkey button. It lives in the
         head, at layout level, for two ordering reasons.
         Layout level: the router only re-executes INLINE page scripts on a
         swap — a `script src` inside the routed main is removed outright
         (`if (s.hasAttribute('src')) { s.remove(); return }`) — so shipped
         from login.stx it vanished the moment you reached /login from
         /register.
         Head, and classic (no defer): login's inline IIFE reads
         window.stacksPasskey the instant it runs, and it runs during body
         parse. A src tag placed after main — or deferred — executes after
         that read, leaving the passkey button permanently hidden. In the
         head it blocks parse and is guaranteed to have run first.
         Costs /register one 5KB file it does not use. --}}
    <script src="/assets/scripts/webauthn-client.js"></script>
    {{-- No <style> block: rule 3 / §11.1. These 54 rules are
         config/crosswind.ts's `authCss()` preflight, scoped to the `auth`
         layout group -- it has to be scoped, because this chrome and
         invite/[uuid].stx and the dashboard sheet all declare `.button`,
         `.brand`, `.field`, `.error` and `.sub`, with different values. The
         five --sso-mask declarations went with their buttons. --}}
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
@yield('content')
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
